        "original_id": "6ff60b1c-e220-5f75-8e4e-0b739e0c1706",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Bangalter, Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo, Gaspar Noé, Monica Bellucci, Vincent Cassel, Albert Dupontel\n- Organizations: Daft Punk, Stardust, Together, Roulé\n- Works: Irréversible\n- Roles: musician, record producer, singer, songwriter, DJ, composer, film director\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Bangalter was born on 3 January 1975 and is a French musician, record producer, singer, songwriter, DJ, composer, and film director.\n- In 1995, Thomas Bangalter founded the French record label Roulé.\n- Thomas Bangalter is best known as one half of the French house music duo Daft Punk alongside Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo.\n- Thomas Bangalter also recorded and released music as a member of Stardust, as a member of Together, and as a solo artist.\n- In 2002, Irréversible was released as a French art psychological horror drama film written and directed by Gaspar Noé.\n- Irréversible stars Monica Bellucci, Vincent Cassel, and Albert Dupontel.\n- Irréversible uses a non-linear narrative and follows two men through the streets of Paris as they seek revenge for a girlfriend who was brutally raped.\n- Thomas Bangalter created compositions for the film Irréversible.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3981e170-85c4-5d72-9981-0c0ea25ccfac",
        "text": "Page: Thomas Bangalter. Sentence: Thomas Bangalter (] ; born 3 January 1975) is a French musician, record producer, singer, songwriter, DJ, composer and film director, best known for being one half of the French house music duo Daft Punk, alongside Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo.\nPage: Thomas Bangalter. Sentence: He has also recorded and released music as a member of the trio Stardust, the duo Together, and as a solo artist including compositions for the film \"Irréversible\".\nPage: Irréversible. Sentence: Irréversible (] ) is a 2002 French art psychological horror drama film written and directed by Gaspar Noé and starring Monica Bellucci, Vincent Cassel, and Albert Dupontel.\nPage: Irréversible. Sentence: The film employs a non-linear narrative and follows two men through the streets of Paris as they seek to avenge a brutally raped girlfriend.\nPage: Roulé. Sentence: Roulé (translating to \"rolled\") is a French record label founded in 1995 by Daft Punk member Thomas Bangalter.",
